course: dictionary
lesson: 6464
title: A rare word for swimming
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Natation is a rare, formal English word that means swimming. You will hardly ever meet it in an English story, so do not panic when it looks unusual.
explain: Look at the clues around it. If the sentence talks about water, a pool or lanes, you can guess it is about swimming. Then check by swapping in the word swimming and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word is much more common in French. «La natation» is the ordinary French word for swimming as a sport or school subject, so you will often see it on signs for «piscine» (pool) and «cours de natation» (swimming lessons).
fact: Natation means the act or art of swimming.
fact: In French, «la natation» means swimming as a sport or school subject.
fact: «Cours de natation» means swimming lessons.
fact: Words ending in -tion are feminine in French: la station, la question, la natation.
fact: To say you go swimming in French, say «je fais de la natation».
exercise: What does natation mean? | *Swimming | Running | Sleeping | Climbing
exercise: «Je fais de la natation le mercredi.» What does this mean? | *I go swimming on Wednesdays | I go cycling on Wednesdays | I am swimming in the sea today
exercise: Which sign shows swimming lessons? | *Cours de natation | Terrain de foot | Salle de judo | Piscine fermée
test: Which article is correct before natation? | *la natation | les natation | le natation
test: In a science book, «natatorial» describes what? | *Animals that swim | Animals that climb trees | Plants that grow in sand | Animals that fly
exam: Which sentence correctly says "I go swimming" in French? | je fais du natation | *je fais de la natation | je fais le natation | je suis natation
